sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2022-tame-27> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "In Xenopus, the action of a single ion channel can induce an eye-specific bioelectric state that creates complete eyes in gut endoderm, spinal cord and posterior tissues, locations where genetic master regulators such as Pax6 are insufficient in vertebrates; bioelectric states thus act as master regulators that evolution can exploit for modular anatomical change.";
    dc:type "experimental-result";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A single ion channel can induce complete ectopic eyes where Pax6 cannot";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “Technological Approach to Mind Everywhere: An Experimentally-Grounded Framework for Understanding Diverse Bodies and Minds”, Frontiers in systems neuroscience (2022), doi:10.3389/fnsys.2022.768201; section “Evolutionary Aspects › Somatic Bioelectrics Reveals the Origin of Complex Cognitive Systems”. Scope: Xenopus laevis embryos misexpressing ion channels"
}
